{{define "main"}}
  <main class="go-Container" id="main-content">
    <div class="go-Content">
      <h1>Install Lyuba</h1>
      <p>Lyuba compiles to Go: you need <a href="https://go.dev/dl/">Go</a> 1.27 or later (the script offers to install it if it is missing).</p>
      <h2>Linux, macOS, Git Bash</h2>
      <pre>curl -fsSL https://pkg.lyuba.dev/install.sh | sh</pre>
      <h2>Windows (PowerShell)</h2>
      <pre>irm https://pkg.lyuba.dev/install.ps1 | iex</pre>
      <p>The script is interactive: it asks before each action (Enter accepts the default). It installs the <code>lyuba</code> command, offers to add the Go binaries folder to your <code>PATH</code>, then gopls (hover, go to definition and completion in your editor), goreleaser (binaries for <code>lyuba publish</code>) and the VS Code extension.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>LYUBA_YES=1</code>: accept every default, no questions (CI)</li>
        <li><code>LYUBA_VERSION=v1.2.3</code>: a specific version</li>
        <li><code>LYUBA_PATH=0</code>: never modify the <code>PATH</code></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Read the script before running it: <a href="/install.sh">install.sh</a>, <a href="/install.ps1">install.ps1</a>.</p>
      <h2>Without the script</h2>
      <pre>go install github.com/GlazKrovi/lyuba/cmd/lyuba@latest</pre>
      <h2>First program</h2>
      <pre>mkdir hello &amp;&amp; cd hello
lyuba init
lyuba run .</pre>
    </div>
  </main>
{{end}}
